From: Nico Marinò <niconotnicko@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Add opt-in monitor-aware software vsync for Wayland

Reuse SoftwareVsyncSource scheduling and its observer-driven lifecycle.
Track monitor hotplug and refresh-rate notifications without polling. Stop
continuous frame callback renewal on both root and native child surfaces.
Keep one-shot map/unmap callbacks and buffer commits intact.

The shared clock follows the fastest connected output, matching the model
of the existing Xrandr software backend. It is not phase-locked to scanout.
The startup preference keeps the original backend available for comparison.

Experimental downstream implementation; not an upstream-approved fix.
Related: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2009606
Related: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1879271
License: MPL-2.0

